  "resources": {
    "costumbres": {
      "c-6f5142d73d9d929f": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-782",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "Some suppose that by these “crumbs’’ are meant the pieces of bread wherewith it was customary at table to wipe the fingers, an act rendered necessary by the practice of conveying the food to the mouth by means of the hand. When the fingers were thus wiped, the fragments of bread…"
      },
      "c-eec8ae7c96bf69f5": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-781",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The steward had general charge of the business of the house, and especial care of the heir. This is referred to in Galatians 4:2 where the word elsewhere rendered “stewards” is translated “governors.” The office is a very ancient one. Abraham had a steward, Eliezer. See Genesis 1…"
      }
    },
